@startuml mecha-charon
' SPEC: _spec/specials/mecha-charon.puml
' purpose: Mecha Charon rename (bishopCharon -> mechaCharon) + ship-collision free-aim redesign — IMPLEMENTED.
!include ../themes/proveo.puml

skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam defaultTextAlignment left

title Mecha Charon Missiles · Rename + Ship-Collision Free Aim

package "packages/starchess-core — rules" {
  component "rules/specials/mechaCharon.ts\ncharonDiagonalSquares (free aim)\ncharonTargetShips (AI kill list)\ncharonStrikeTarget (kill check)\ncharonRayEdge (fizzle edge)\nplacementAfterMechaCharon()" as RULE <<app>>
  component "rules/validation.ts\nbishopSnipe case: any Mecha diagonal queues\nCharon requires mecha / needs aim square /\naim must be on a Mecha diagonal" as VAL <<error>>
  component "resolve/submit-turn.ts\nfire-and-forget: paid gas resolves\nfrom queued square (no live Mecha needed)\nkill iff aim is first ship for action color\nF origin rewrites only on own C move" as RES <<app>>
  component "ai/strategies/captures.ts\n+ strategic twin + plans/stacks.ts\n1 candidate per killable ship, CHARON_COMBO kept" as AI <<app>>
}

package "apps/starchess — presentation" {
  component "specials/arms/mechaCharon.ts\nmechaCharonArm: all diagonals, click-to-pick\nnever rejects for lack of ships" as ARM <<app>>
  component "specials/copy.ts[b]\nMecha / Charon Booster Missiles\nany diagonal — first ship detonates\nelse flies off-board" as COPY <<app>>
  component "animations/mechaCharon.ts\nsymbol MECHA_CHARON, value bishopCharon\ncue id + OPEN_BISHOP_SNIPE frozen\nfizzle: extended span, no impact burst" as VFX <<app>>
}

database "SCFEN Q:\nB/F=charonMissiles:from:to\nwire kind frozen" as WIRE <<db>>

RULE ARROW_MAIN VAL : diagonal set
VAL ARROW_MAIN RES : queued aim
RULE ARROW_MAIN AI : killable list
ARM ARROW_MAIN RULE : diagonals via core index
ARM ARROW_MAIN WIRE : queue B/F charonMissiles
RES ARROW_MAIN WIRE : placement delete on kill
ARM ARROW_OPTIONAL VFX : attack + death / fizzle cues

note right of RULE
  **Ray walk (implemented).**
  4 Mecha diagonals, step to edge.
  Aim set: every on-board diagonal square
  (""charonDiagonalSquares"", sorted).
  Kill (""charonStrikeTarget""): aim holds an enemy
  Ship (q) with no ship strictly between —
  i.e. aim is the first ship on its ray.
  Non-ships (p/n/b/r/k, either color; mines are
  not on the placement map) are transparent.
  Ally ships screen but never die (no ally-fire).
  Engine stays omniscient; fog filters highlights only.
end note

note right of VAL
  **Superseded behavior.**
  ""charonTargetQueen"": exactly one enemy queen
  anywhere on the diagonals, blockers ignored,
  single Square|null. Replaced by free aim +
  first-ship strike check (clean cut, no queen API).
end note

note bottom
  **Rename map (wire frozen).**
  bishopCharon.ts → mechaCharon.ts; charonTargetQueen* →
  charonTargetShips* + charonDiagonalSquares* + charonStrikeTarget +
  charonRayEdge (clean cut, no queen); placementAfterCharon →
  placementAfterMechaCharon; CHARON_GAS_COST + MECHA_CHARON_GAS_COST
  alias; arms/charonMissiles.ts → arms/mechaCharon.ts;
  bishopSnipeArm → mechaCharonArm; animations/bishopCharon.ts →
  animations/mechaCharon.ts; BISHOP_CHARON → MECHA_CHARON (string
  value ""bishopCharon"" frozen); copy [b] rewritten to free aim;
  queen → BattleShip in q copy.
  SCFEN kind ""charonMissiles"", store action ""OPEN_BISHOP_SNIPE"",
  VFX cue ""bishopCharon"" stay frozen for replay compat.
  ----
  **2nd gas phase (F) dynamics.** B evaluates on turn-open placement;
  F on post-C placement. F Charon now projects attack+death cues
  (previously B-only). Ally ships screen; empty diagonals are
  selectable and fizzle visibly instead of rejecting.
  ----
  **Decided (human).**
  R1 F-drift / empty ray → fizzle with off-board flight animation
  (extended volley span to ray edge + 2.5 cells, no impact burst,
  no death cue) instead of silent no-op or error.
  R2 public API clean cut (no queen names).
  R3 highlight-all + click-to-pick on any diagonal square.
  R4 (human) fire-and-forget over dead-actor fizzle: the Mecha need not
  be alive at resolve — paid gas resolves from the queued square using
  the action color (differs from classical/F-gas dead-actor skips).
  F origin rewrites to post-C square only when the unit's own classical
  moved it; otherwise the shot stays on its arming square (no borrowing
  another unit's square).
  ----
  **Verification.** Core ""bishop/mechaCharon.test.ts"": fly-through,
  ally screen, enemy screen, multi-ray, free-aim diagonals (13 from
  d4), validation accept/reject, kill, F-fizzle, ray edge.
  AI ""ai/charonHunt.test.ts"": pre-21 B insta, post-21 F guess as C+F,
  income (not turn) gating, predictor determinism, composer screen-drops;
  ""tactics/weightOrdering.test.ts"" pins INSTA > COMBO > GUESS×rate.
  Presentation ""specials/pieceArms.test.ts"" (free-aim arm),
  ""boardInput/useBoardInputCoverage"" + ""matchReducer.actions""
  (targets list), ""timelinePlayer"" (B kill cues), ""tutorialScript""
  (frozen charonMissiles SCFEN). Full core + app suites green.
  ----
  **Adjutant hunt (two-mode, naive + strategic twin).**
  Gate ""enemyCanJump"" = enemy gasIncome ≥ 3 (never the turn number).
  Pre-jump: B insta-targets at killable first-ships, bonus CHARON_INSTA
  3_200 (near-guaranteed — B resolves before either classical and no
  enemy B jump is affordable). Post-jump: F guesses at top-3 mirrored
  warp predictions per (mecha, ship) — center + safety + king-menace,
  no vision filter (mechas see board-wide) — filtered to free-aim
  diagonals and strike-verified on the predicted board, committed via
  C+F ""charonForwardStacks"" (mecha stays put; own classical must not
  occupy/screen the aim), bonus CHARON_GUESS 2_000 × HIT_RATE 0.4
  (≈800, hotter by human call). Never both modes in one turn.
  F singles commit only inside C+F stacks (orchestrators exclude lone-F);
  partners come from top-scored classicals (cap 16) that leave the aim clear.
end note
@enduml
